This repository holds a couple of Python scripts built to streamline neuroimaging workflows. They handle everything from raw anatomical surface reconstruction using Charm to running personalized SimNIBS tDCS simulations and extracting ROI stats.
1. run_charm_T1-T2.py
Batch script that automates head mesh creation using Charm.   
  What it does: 
    Loops through subject directories (sub-XXXX/ses-base/anat/) looking for T1w and T2w structural scans.   
    Skips completed work: Automatically checks if an m2m folder already exists for a subject so it doesn't re-run charm unnecessarily.   
    Clean execution: Ignores hidden/corrupted macOS files (like ._*) and fires off charm subjectXXXX <T1> <T2> --forceqform directly in the subject folder.  
